
# .cursorrules — Nexa ERP (final)

---

alwaysApply: true

---

project: Nexa ERP

baseline:

  stack: Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + PNPM 10 + Node 20 + Prisma (Neon/Postgres) + Vercel

  root: apps/web

  productionUrl: https://app.nexaai.co.uk

  auth: next-auth (credentials + Google + Microsoft + OTP)

  ui: approved Nexa ERP layout (sidebar, header/breadcrumbs, KPI band, AI Engine bar at bottom)

nonNegotiables:

  - Do NOT create /pages routes. App Router only.

  - Do NOT change package manager. PNPM 10 only.

  - Do NOT edit production .env or Vercel prod env; only output names.

  - Do NOT weaken CSP/HSTS/rate limits.

  - Do NOT touch apps/web/app/(auth)/** or NextAuth config unless current task explicitly says so.

  - Do NOT change the approved login layout.

  - Do NOT commit code with "PLACEHOLDER" or "TODO UI".

protectedFiles:

  - .env

  - .env.*

  - prisma/schema.prisma

  - apps/web/app/(auth)/**

  - apps/web/middleware.ts

  - vercel.json

  - docs/**

  - ops/**

globalRules:

  - Every authenticated page must use the shared Nexa layout and render the AI Engine bar.

  - Every query must be tenant-aware once tenancy is re-tightened.

  - Every schema change must produce: 1) schema diff, 2) prisma migrate command, 3) backfill/seed instructions, 4) Neon/staging apply steps.

  - Every auth or layout change must add/update Playwright smoke tests.

  - Output file list + CLI commands for me to run.

